--TEST--
`stream` classifies its statement text exactly as `query` does, so the member that holds a connection open is no easier a way into a database than the one that does not — `rule:security/sink-predicate`, `rule:core-classes/db-statement-members` and `rule:core-classes/db-parameters`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `rule:core-classes/db-statement-members` gives `stream` and `query` one signature and one binding rule,
// and the sink classification is half of that signature: the statement text is
// a sink on both, so a value from outside the process cannot be written into
// it, and a bound parameter accepts the same value freely.
//
// This is worth asserting on its own member rather than inferred from `query`'s
// case, because a row is where the classification lives — a `Qual::Neutral`
// pasted into this one would compile, run, and be a whole injection surface
// that no other case in the corpus looks at.
tainted string $outside = "ada";

var $db = Core\Db::connect("main");

// The refusal. There is no escaper to launder the value with, here or on any
// other `Core\Db` member: binding is the mechanism. Naming the walk is enough —
// the statement is written at the call and not at the first row.
var $refused = $db->stream($outside, []);

// And the way through, which is the same value at the same statement — a sink
// with no admitting spelling beside it would be a member no program can pass
// data to.
var $bound = $db->stream("select id from accounts where owner = ?", [$outside]);

// The classification is on the row and not on the receiver, and `rule:classes/no-traits`'s
// delegation means the row is declared twice — so the refusal is asked of the
// other declaring class as well. A `Core\Db\Transaction` that accepted a
// `tainted` statement would be an injection surface reachable from inside every
// transaction in an application, which is where the writes are.
$db->transaction(fn (Core\Db\Transaction $tx): void => {
    $tx->stream($outside, []);
});
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0401]: expected `string`, found `tainted string`
   --> case.nvs:18:28
%A
error: aborting due to 2 errors
